# Rank 1124 / CVE-2026-40034: gix-submodule's File::update had to refuse an
# `update = !<command>` value coming from the repository-controlled
# .gitmodules file, and guarded it by asking the wrong question: whether ANY
# `submodule.<name>` section existed from a source other than .gitmodules --
# true after any normal `git submodule` workflow writes
# `submodule.<name>.url` into .git/config -- instead of asking where the
# value it actually read came from. The string accessor walks the merged
# sources and falls through to .gitmodules whenever the local override
# section does not itself set `update`, so a command from .gitmodules passed
# once a local override section existed. Real git refuses the same state.
#
# The fix reads through `string_filter` with a callback that records, at the
# moment of the read, whether that read's own source is the .gitmodules
# meta, and refuses the command on that flag. Both revisions carry the same
# `std::ptr::eq` meta comparison; what changed is only what it is applied to.
#
# ATTENTION, vocabulary gap, re-measured at scanner feae1e651. Three
# --cache off scans of gix-submodule per revision report the identical
# single unrelated VYQL-MEM-006 row (access.rs:42, a HashSet insert in
# names()), and full-repo scans of both revisions yield identical
# 1367-finding header sets, so nothing shipped since detects it; the
# `-flags only` view is identical too. code.ProtocolStateReview
# (VYQL-AUTH-082) now reaches Rust through the strict-kex binding, whose
# shape needs NEWKEYS/KEXINIT spellings. Probe bindings measured every
# discriminator the fix diff leaves: keying on `Update::Command` +
# `sections_by_name` discriminates 1 -> 0 with zero collateral on the whole
# tree, but is this incident's own spelling of the wrong question -- the
# same `sections_by_name` iteration asks the right one 130 lines earlier in
# names(), which filters by `s.meta().source == META_MARKER` -- and
# negating on `string_filter`/`value_is_from_modules_file` keys on the
# fixing commit's own layout. The `!command` parse into Update::Command
# (config.rs TryFrom) is byte-identical in both revisions, so keys on it
# fire on both. The documented invariant (Update::Command is "only allowed
# if the value is coming from an override") needs the read's own provenance
# across gix-config's source merge, a value-level fact no layer emits, and
# the tree holds no execution site for the command (gix's submodule
# update() only delegates here), so no taint route exists either.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap, both revisions rejected.

test "rank1124: the guard asks whether ANY foreign section exists, not where the value read came from"
  lang rust
  file access.rs
  reject VYQL-AUTH-082
  code
  ```
  impl File {
      pub fn update(&self, name: &BStr) -> Result<Option<Update>, config::update::Error> {
          let value: Update = match self.config.string(&format!("submodule.{name}.update")) {
              Some(v) => v.as_ref().try_into().map_err(|()| config::update::Error::Invalid {
                  submodule: name.to_owned(),
                  actual: v.into_owned(),
              })?,
              None => return Ok(None),
          };

          if let Update::Command(cmd) = &value {
              let ours = self.config.meta();
              let has_value_from_foreign_section = self
                  .config
                  .sections_by_name("submodule")
                  .into_iter()
                  .flatten()
                  .any(|s| s.header().subsection_name() == Some(name) && !std::ptr::eq(s.meta(), ours));
              if !has_value_from_foreign_section {
                  return Err(config::update::Error::CommandForbiddenInModulesConfiguration {
                      submodule: name.to_owned(),
                      actual: cmd.to_owned(),
                  });
              }
          }
          Ok(Some(value))
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1124: the guard asks whether the value actually read came from .gitmodules"
  lang rust
  file access.rs
  reject VYQL-AUTH-082
  code
  ```
  impl File {
      pub fn update(&self, name: &BStr) -> Result<Option<Update>, config::update::Error> {
          let mut value_is_from_modules_file = None;
          let our_meta = self.config.meta();
          let value: Update = match self.config.string_filter(&format!("submodule.{name}.update"), |meta| {
              value_is_from_modules_file = Some(std::ptr::eq(meta, our_meta));
              true
          }) {
              Some(v) => v.as_ref().try_into().map_err(|()| config::update::Error::Invalid {
                  submodule: name.to_owned(),
                  actual: v.into_owned(),
              })?,
              None => return Ok(None),
          };

          if let Update::Command(cmd) = &value {
              if value_is_from_modules_file.unwrap_or_default() {
                  return Err(config::update::Error::CommandForbiddenInModulesConfiguration {
                      submodule: name.to_owned(),
                      actual: cmd.to_owned(),
                  });
              }
          }
          Ok(Some(value))
      }
  }
  ```
